cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Mirab in your work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Mirab: water distribution and stormwater modeling with EPANET, SWMM and SWMM5+"
authors:
  - family-names: Madadi
    given-names: Ehsan
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/ehsanMa86/Mirab"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23679047
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.23679047
    description: All versions (concept DOI); resolves to the latest version.
url: "https://ehsanma86.github.io/Mirab/"
abstract: >-
  Mirab is a free, cross-platform desktop application for modeling water
  distribution and stormwater systems. It puts EPA EPANET 2.2, OWA EPANET 2.3,
  EPANET-MSX 2.0, EPA SWMM 5.2 and the SWMM5+ finite-volume solver behind one
  interface, with live results, calibration, scenarios, resilience metrics,
  GIS exchange, a command-line interface and a Python package.
keywords:
  - EPANET
  - SWMM
  - SWMM5+
  - water distribution
  - stormwater
  - urban drainage
  - hydraulic modeling
